---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Method" description="How I take an AI idea from business problem to adopted solution.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 8px">
      <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
      <h1>From business problem to adopted AI solution</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The same five steps apply in every domain. What changes is the vocabulary, the data and the risks.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <h3>Discover</h3>
        <p>Map stakeholders, run pain-point workshops, and build a longlist of AI ideas tied to revenue, cost or efficiency. Output: stakeholder map, as-is process, opportunity list.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <h3>Prioritise</h3>
        <p>Score every idea on business value, data readiness, feasibility, risk and adoption ease, so the first pilot is chosen on evidence. Output: weighted scoring matrix and a one-page business case.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <h3>Define</h3>
        <p>Write requirements engineers can build from: user stories, acceptance criteria, data requirements, and AI-specific needs such as accuracy targets, evaluation and human-in-the-loop rules. Output: requirements package, risk register.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <h3>Prototype</h3>
        <p>Test the riskiest assumption quickly with data analysis, an LLM workflow or a small demo, before anyone commits to a full build. Output: working prototype and evaluation results.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <h3>Adopt</h3>
        <p>Plan the change: training, rollout, measures of success, and a feedback loop so the solution keeps improving. Output: adoption plan and KPI dashboard.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Technical edge</h2>
    <div class="grid three">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Data</h3>
        <p class="muted">SQL, Excel, Power BI. Python for data analysis (currently learning, practised through the projects on this site).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>AI</h3>
        <p class="muted">Prompt design, RAG concepts, LLM workflow design, evaluation planning, responsible-AI checklists.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Systems</h3>
        <p class="muted">Requirements for enterprise platforms (including IBM Maximo), APIs and integrations, process and data modelling (BPMN, UML).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
